PATCH 177: thread FUN_0000_47e0's dropped device-method register args (asm 0x47e0-0x4822).

47e0 is the in-mission display-list PAINT dispatch.  Its four indirect far method-vector calls dropped
every register arg (the standard __allregs indirect-method-vector class).  Threaded per the asm + each
callee's contract (patch 174 already threaded the 5th, c6a8=2595):
 - [d594](al=1)  asm 0x47e0: context-SELECT the paint object (mga 0x2cc7 wrapper -> 0x2ccd, patch 176).
 - [c560](ax=8,cx=ds,bx=0x7a42)  asm 0x47e6: mga 0x0310 resource-open -> descriptor DGROUP:0x7a42
   (its word0 = the off-screen fill-buffer segment 2595 then fills).
 - [c68c](al=0xff,bx=0x7ac0,si=0x7a42)  asm 0x47f9: MGAVIDEO offset-0 no-op; args inert but threaded.
 - [d594](al=0)  asm 0x481c: context-SELECT restore.

Behaviour-neutral for the 19 verify flows: d594/c560/c68c are 0/uninstalled in the menu (gdb-verified),
so fist_icall_far(0) still traps no-op regardless of the threaded args.  re_out sources stay pristine.

